     ## 6. List Endpoints Return Paginated[0m[2m Data
     
     All list endpoints (e.g., `GET /v2/tasks`) no longer return a bare array of items. Instead, they return a paginated envelope object that includes the `items` array, `total` count, and[0m[2m a `next_cursor` for pagination.
     
     ### Before (v1) - Response for `GET /tasks`
     
[0m[2m```[0m[2mjson
     [
       {"id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created[0m[2m_at": "..."},
       {"id": 2, "title": "Ship v1", "done": true, "created_at": "..."}
     ]
[0m[2m```
     
     ### After (v2) - Response for[0m[2m `GET /v2/tasks`
     
[0m[2m```[0m[2mjson
     {
       "items": [
         {"id": "a1b2c3d4-...", "title": "Buy milk", "completed": false, "project_[0m[2mid": "...", "created_at": "..."},
         {"id": "b2c3d4e5-...", "title": "Ship v1", "completed": true, "project_id": "...", "created_[0m[2mat": "..."}
       ],
       "total": 42,
       "next_cursor": "cursor_xyz"
     }
[0m[2m```
     
     To fetch the next page, you would pass `?cursor=<next_cursor[0m[2m>` as a query parameter. You can also specify a `limit` for the number of results per page (default 20).
     
     ### Code Example
     
     **Before (v1) - Listing tasks**
     
[0m[2m```[0m[2mpython
     import requests
     
     api_[0m[2mkey = "your_v1_api_key"
     headers = {"X-Auth-Token": api_key}
     response = requests.get("https://api.zrb.com/tasks", headers=headers)[0m[2m
     tasks = response.json() # Direct array of tasks
     for task in tasks:
         print(f"Task ID: {task['id']}, Title: {task['title']}, Done: {task['done']}")
[0m[2m```
     
     **After (v2) - Listing tasks**
     
     ```[0m[2mpython
     import requests
     
     api_token = "your_v2_api_token"
     headers = {"Authorization": f"Bearer {api_token}"}
[0m[2mbase_url = "https://api.zrb.com/v2/tasks"
     
     # First page
     response = requests.get(base_url, headers=headers)
     tasks_data = response.json() #[0m[2m Paginated envelope
     tasks = tasks_data["items"]
     for task in tasks:
         print(f"Task ID: {task['id']}, Title: {task['title']}, Completed: {task['completed']}")
     
     # Fetching[0m[2m the next page (if available)
     next_cursor = tasks_data.get("next_cursor")
     if next_cursor:
         print(f"\nFetching next page with cursor: {next_cursor}")
         response[0m[2m = requests.get(f"{base_url}?cursor={next_cursor}", headers=headers)
         next_page_data = response.json()
         next_page_tasks = next_page_data["items[0m[2m"]
         for task in next_page_tasks:
             print(f"Task ID: {task['id']}, Title: {task['title']}, Completed: {task['completed']}")
[0m[2m```
     
